{"geneId":"1139","symbol":"CHRNA7","description":"cholinergic receptor nicotinic alpha 7 subunit","taxId":"9606","taxname":"Homo sapiens","type":"PROTEIN_CODING","orientation":"plus","commonName":"human","chromosomes":["15"],"nomenclatureAuthority":{"authority":"HGNC","identifier":"HGNC:1960"},"swissProtAccessions":["P36544"],"ensemblGeneIds":["ENSG00000175344"],"omimIds":["118511"],"synonyms":["nAChR7","NACHRA7","a7nAChR","CHRNA7-2"],"referenceStandards":[{"geneRange":{"accessionVersion":"NG_009216.2","range":[{"begin":"5034","end":"147537","orientation":"plus"}]},"type":"REFSEQ_GENE"}],"annotations":[{"assemblyAccession":"GCF_000001405.40","assemblyName":"GRCh38.p14","annotationName":"GCF_000001405.40-RS_2025_08","annotationReleaseDate":"2025-08-01","genomicLocations":[{"genomicAccessionVersion":"NC_000015.10","sequenceName":"15","genomicRange":{"begin":"32030483","end":"32173018","orientation":"plus"}},{"genomicAccessionVersion":"NT_187660.1","sequenceName":"15","genomicRange":{"begin":"4315603","end":"4458353","orientation":"plus"}},{"genomicAccessionVersion":"NW_011332701.1","sequenceName":"15","genomicRange":{"begin":"4203151","end":"4345901","orientation":"plus"}},{"genomicAccessionVersion":"NW_012132920.1","sequenceName":"15","genomicRange":{"begin":"355066","end":"497808","orientation":"minus"}}]},{"assemblyAccession":"GCF_009914755.1","assemblyName":"T2T-CHM13v2.0","annotationName":"GCF_009914755.1-RS_2025_08","annotationReleaseDate":"2025-08-01","genomicLocations":[{"genomicAccessionVersion":"NC_060939.1","sequenceName":"15","genomicRange":{"begin":"29824630","end":"29967342","orientation":"plus"}}]}],"transcriptCount":29,"proteinCount":28,"transcriptTypeCounts":[{"type":"PROTEIN_CODING","count":2},{"type":"NON_CODING","count":1},{"type":"PROTEIN_CODING_MODEL","count":26}],"geneGroups":[{"id":"1139","method":"NCBI Ortholog"}],"summary":[{"description":"The nicotinic acetylcholine receptors (nAChRs) are members of a superfamily of ligand-gated ion channels that mediate fast signal transmission at synapses. The nAChRs are thought to be hetero-pentamers composed of homologous subunits. The proposed structure for each subunit is a conserved N-terminal extracellular domain followed by three conserved transmembrane domains, a variable cytoplasmic loop, a fourth conserved transmembrane domain, and a short C-terminal extracellular region. The protein encoded by this gene forms a homo-oligomeric channel, displays marked permeability to calcium ions and is a major component of brain nicotinic receptors that are blocked by, and highly sensitive to, alpha-bungarotoxin. Once this receptor binds acetylcholine, it undergoes an extensive change in conformation that affects all subunits and leads to opening of an ion-conducting channel across the plasma membrane. This gene is located in a region identified as a major susceptibility locus for juvenile myoclonic epilepsy and a chromosomal location involved in the genetic transmission of schizophrenia. An evolutionarily recent partial duplication event in this region results in a hybrid containing sequence from this gene and a novel FAM7A gene. Alternative splicing results in multiple transcript variants. [provided by RefSeq, Feb 2012]"}],"geneOntology":{"assignedBy":"GOA","molecularFunctions":[{"name":"acetylcholine binding","goId":"GO:0042166","evidenceCode":"IDA","qualifier":"enables","reference":{"pmids":["8145738"]}},{"name":"acetylcholine receptor activity","goId":"GO:0015464","evidenceCode":"IDA","qualifier":"enables","reference":{"pmids":["8906617"]}},{"name":"acetylcholine receptor activity","goId":"GO:0015464","evidenceCode":"IEA","qualifier":"enables"},{"name":"acetylcholine-gated monoatomic cation-selective channel activity","goId":"GO:0022848","evidenceCode":"IBA","qualifier":"contributes_to"},{"name":"acetylcholine-gated monoatomic cation-selective channel activity","goId":"GO:0022848","evidenceCode":"IDA","qualifier":"contributes_to","reference":{"pmids":["38161283"]}},{